doesn't get that carryover unless it was from the tens.\n\nWait, the carryover from the tens place is 1, so when adding the hundreds:\n\n6 (first number) + 1 (second number) + 1 (carryover from tens) = 8. So that's correct, 8 with no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 0 (first) +9 (second) =9. No carryover. So digit 9.\n\nTen thousands place:1 (first) +9 (second) =10. So digit 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:3 (first) +9 (second) =12, plus the carryover 1 makes 13. So 13. So here, the digit is 3, and carryover 1.\n\nSince there are no more digits, that carryover becomes a new digit in the millions place.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:0\n\nHundreds:8\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nMillions:1\n\nSo the total is 1,309,801.\n\nWait, let me confirm this by another method. Let's add the numbers in parts.\n\n310,609 + 999,192.\n\nMaybe break them down:\n\n310,609 + 999,192 = (300,000 + 10,609) + (900,000 + 99,192)\n\nAdding the large parts first: 300k +900k=1,200,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts:10,609 +99,192.\n\n10,609 +99,192. Let's compute that:\n\n10,609\n\n+99,192\n\n=?\n\nAdding:\n\nOnes:9+2=11, so 1 carryover 1.\n\nTens:0+9=9 +1=10 →0 carryover1.\n\nHundreds:6+1=7 +1=8.\n\nThousands:0+9=9.\n\nTen thousands:1+9=10 →0 carryover1.\n\nSo that gives 109,801.\n\nWait, so 10,609 +99,192 = 109,801?\n\nWait 10,609 + 99,192:\n\n10,609 + 99,192:\n\nLet me do it step by step:\n\n10,609\n\n+99,192\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:9+2=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTens:0+9=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:6+1=7 +1=8 →8, no carry.\n\nThousands:0+9=9 →9.\n\nTen-thousands:1+9=10 →0 carryover1.\n\nSo the result is 109,801. Wait but adding 10,609 +99,192:\n\nWait 10,609 + 99,192. Let me do it another way. 10,609 + 99,192 = (10,000 + 609) + (99,000 + 192) = (10,000 +99,000) + (609+192)= 109,000 + 801= 109,801. Yes that's correct.\n\nSo total sum is 1,200,000 +109,801 =1,309,801. Which matches the previous result