nds), 8 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\n619,120 is 6 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8. Write 8.\n\nTens place: 8 + 2 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 1 = 2, plus the carried 1 makes 3. Write 3.\n\nThousands place: 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 + 1 = 3, plus the carried 1 makes 4. Write 4.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 10.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 1,047,308.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n428,188 + 600,000 = 1,028,188\n\nThen add 19,120 (since 619,120 - 600,000 = 19,120):\n\n1,028,188 + 19,120 = ?\n\n1,028,188 + 10,000 = 1,038,188\n\n1,038,188 + 9,120 = 1,047,308. Okay, same result.\n\nAnother check: using calculator-like addition.\n\n428,188\n\n+619,120\n\nAdding digit by digit again:\n\nOnes: 8+0=8\n\nTens:8+2=10 (0 carry 1)\n\nHundreds:1+1 +1=3\n\nThousands:8+9=17 (7 carry 1)\n\nTen-thousands:2+1 +1=4\n\nHundred-thousands:4+6=10.\n\nSo yes, 1,047,308. Looks correct.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 980794 and 805499?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n4. The ones place: 2 + 5 = 0.\n4. The tens place: 5 + 0 = 87 (write 5, carry over 2).\n5. The hundreds place: 5 + 8 + 6 (carry) = 1.\n1. The thousands place: 7 + 7 = 66 (write 0, carry over 5).\n4. The ten-thousands place: 1 + 6 + 8 (carry) = 3.\n7. The hundred-thousands place: 2 + 1 = 45.\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is "]]
