ns: 0 + 0 = 0 (but carryover later)\n\nHundred thousands: 3 (from first number) +9 (second) =12 \u2192 2 with carryover 1.\n\nWait, perhaps better to do:\n\n352,696  \n+992,339  \n= ?\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes: 6+9=15 \u21925, carry 1.\n\nTens:9+3=12 +1=13 \u21923, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:6+3=9 +1=10 \u21920, carry 1.\n\nThousands:2+2=4 +1=5 \u21925, no carry.\n\nTen-thousands:5+9=14 \u21924, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:3+9=12 +1=13 \u21923, carry 1.\n\nMillions: carryover 1.\n\nThus the total is 1,345,035. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 1,345,035. The reasoning steps are as above.",
