 might have messed up the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more clearly:\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 0 + 8 = 8\nTens: 0 + 2 = 2\nHundreds: 5 + 9 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\nThousands: 9 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\nTen thousands: 5 + 8 +1 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\nHundred thousands: 8 +7 +1 =16 (write 6, carry 1)\nMillions: the carryover 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,640,428? Wait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as is:\n\n859,500 + 780,928.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n800,000 + 700,000 = 1,500,000\n\n59,500 + 80,928 = ?\n\n59,500 + 80,000 = 139,500\n\nThen add the remaining 928: 139,500 + 928 = 140,428\n\nAdding that to the 1,500,000 gives 1,500,000 + 140,428 = 1,640,428. Okay, that matches. So the sum should be 1,640,428. Wait, but when I first thought of the places, I thought maybe I made an error in the thousands place? Let me check again the digit-by-digit:\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n859500 is 8 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nWait wait, hold on, maybe I misaligned the digits. Let me write both numbers with their place values properly.\n\nWait, 859,500 is:\n\nDigit places (from right):\n\nOnes: 0\n\nTens: 0\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nThousands: 9\n\nTen thousands: 5\n\nHundred thousands: 8\n\nWait, no, actually, 859,500:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nThe number is 8 5 9 , 5 0 0. So commas separate every three digits. So:\n\nHundred thousands: 8\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:0\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nMillions place: 0 (since it's a 6-digit number)\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:0\n\nOnes:0\n\nThe other number is 780,928:\n\n7 8 0 , 9 2 8.\n\nSo:\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:0\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:2\n\nOnes:8\n\nSo when adding:\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:\n\n\u20038 5 9 5 0 0\n\n+7 8 0 9 2 8\n\n---------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 0 +8 =8\n\nTens:0 +2=2\n\nHundreds:5 +9=14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\nThousands place:9 (from first number) +0 (second number) +1 (carry) =10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\nTen thousands place:5 (first) +8 (second) +1 (carry) =14 (write 4, carry1)\n\nHundred thousands place:8 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carry) =16 (write 6, carry1)\n\nMillions place: the carryover 1.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1,640,428. So that's correct. Therefore, the answer is 1,640,428. I think that's right.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 472056 and 155361?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n4. The ones place: 5 + 6 = 0  .\n9. The tens place: 7 + 5 = 0  .\n7. The hundreds place: 0 + 1 = 68 (Write down 5, carry over 7)  .\n2. The thousands place: 8 + 8 + 8 (carry) = 34 (Write down 9, carry over 8)  .\n9. The ten thousands place: 9 + 2 + 4 (carry) = 26 (Write down 5, carry over 7)  .\n5. The hundred thousands place: 2 + 6 + 0 (carry) = 33 (Write down 0, carry over 5)  .\n8. The millions place: 5 (carry over)  .\n\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is "]] 27%|##7       | 137/500 [39:00<2:17:12, 22.68s/it]
