step by step more carefully. Let me try again:\n\nNumbers are:\n\n  991841\n+ 139758\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9. Correct.\n\nTens: 4 +5 =9. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 8 +7 =15. So 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: The first number has 1 (from 991,841: the thousands digit is the fourth from the right, which is 1?), wait maybe I need to check the digit positions again.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers with commas for clarity:\n\n991,841 is 9 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\n139,758 is 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo aligning:\n\n        9 9 1 8 4 1\n      + 1 3 9 7 5 8\n      ----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n1+8=9 (ones place).\n\nTens: 4+5=9 (tens place).\n\nHundreds:8+7=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:1 (from first number) +9 (from second) =10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. So write 1 here and carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:9 (from first number) +3 (from second) =12, plus carried 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place:9 (from first) +1 (from second)=10, plus carried 1 is 11. So write 1 here and carryover 1 to the millions place.\n\nSo the total would be 1 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 9 (ones). \n\nSo combining all digits: 1,131,599?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step:\n\n991,841 + 100,000 = 1,091,841\n\nThen add 39,758: 1,091,841 + 39,758 = ?\n\n1,091,841 + 30,000 = 1,121,841\n\n1,121,841 +9,758 = 1,131,599. \n\nHmm, same result. So maybe the first calculation was correct. \n\nWait, but let me do it digit by digit again:\n\nAdding the thousands place again:\n\nFirst number's thousands digit is 1 (since 991,841 is 9 (100k), 9 (10k), 1 (1k), then 800+40+1). The second number's thousands digit is 9 (from 139,758: 1 (100k), 3 (10k), 9 (1k)...).