ld be 1,101,937. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 6+1=7 ✔️\n\nTens:6+7=13 ✔️ (3 with carryover 1)\n\nHundreds:8+0+1=9 ✔️\n\nThousands:2+9=11 ✔️ (1 with carryover 1)\n\nTen-thousands:0+9+1=10 ✔️ (0 with carryover 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:8+2+1=11 ✔️ (1 with carryover 1)\n\nMillions: the carryover 1. So total is 1,101,937. Yep, that seems right.\n</think>Let's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n7. The ones place: 3 + 4 = 9.\n5. The tens place: 1 + 0 = 95, write down 6 and carry over 8.\n1. The hundreds place: 9 + 8 + 3 (carry over) = 1.\n0. The thousands place: 6 + 5 = 70, write down 4 and carry over 0.\n4. The ten thousands place: 1 + 2 + 7 (carry over) = 77, write down 4 and carry over 8.\n5. The hundred thousands place: 5 + 8 + 5 (carry over) = 48, write down 3 and carry over 5.\n0. The final carry over: 6.. Therefore, the answer is "]]
