messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 697687 and 681331?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>Okay, I need to add 697,687 and 681,331. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly.\n\nFirst, let's line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n\u2003697,687\n+681,331\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 7 and 1. Adding those gives 8. So, I write down 8 in the ones place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 8 and 3. 8 plus 3 is 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 3, plus the carried over 1. 6 + 3 is 9, plus 1 makes 10. Again, that's a two-digit number. So, I write 0 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 7 and 1, plus the carried over 1. 7 + 1 is 8, plus 1 gives 9. So, I put 9 in the thousands place. No carry-over here.\n\nNext is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 9 and 8. Adding those together gives 17. Wait, 9 + 8 is 17. So I need to write down 7 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 6 and 6, plus the carried over 1. 6 + 6 is 12, plus 1 makes 13. So that's 3 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there's no higher place, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting all the digits together, the sum should be 1,379,020. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the carrying over. Starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 7+1=8 ✔️\n\nTens:8+3=11 ✔️ (with carryover)\n\nHundreds:6+3+1=10 ✔️ (carryover again)\n\nThousands:7+1+1=9 ✔️\n\nTen-thousands:9+8=17 ✔️ (carryover 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:6+6+1=13 ✔️\n\nMillions:1 from the carryover. So total is 1,379,020. That seems right.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 473308 and 423912?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n9. The ones place: 0 + 2 = 1.\n9. The tens place: 6 + 5 = 86 (write 7, carry over 6).\n0. The hundreds place: 4 + 9 + 0 (carry) = 69 (write 5, carry over 3).\n6. The thousands place: 4 + 5 + 0 (carry) = 5.\n2. The ten-thousands place: 1 + 7 = 95 (write 3, carry over 6).\n5. The hundred-thousands place: 1 + 0 + 0 (carry) = 81 (write 9, carry over 4).\n5. The millions place: 8 (carry).\n\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is "]]
