lace.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,661,368. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes with the carries. Hmm, starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 1+7=8 ✔️  \nTens:1+5=6 ✔️  \nHundreds:8+5=13 ✔️ (carry 1)  \nThousands:9+1+1=11 ✔️ (carry 1)  \nTen thousands:7+8+1=16 ✔️ (carry 1)  \nHundred thousands:6+9+1=16 ✔️ (carry 1)  \nMillions:1 carried over. So total is 1,661,368. Yep, that seems right.\n</think>Let's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n4. The ones place: 6 + 5 = 5.\n7. The tens place: 6 + 3 = 3.\n4. The hundreds place: 3 + 3 = 01, write down 5 and carry over 9.\n7. The thousands place: 6 + 6 + 6 (carry over) = 75, write down 3 and carry over 9.\n6. The ten thousands place: 8 + 5 + 6 (carry over) = 08, write down 1 and carry over 7.\n7. The hundred thousands place: 9 + 2 + 0 (carry over) = 07, write down 8 and carry over 6.\n4. The final carry over: 7.. Therefore, the answer is "]]
