ds:1\n\nHundred thousands:6\n\nPlus the carryover 1 in the millions place.\n\nSo the total sum is 1 6 1 6 1 5 0? Wait, let me arrange them properly.\n\nWait, the digits from the addition steps:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n0 (ones)\n\n5 (tens)\n\n1 (hundreds)\n\n6 (thousands)\n\n1 (ten thousands)\n\n6 (hundred thousands)\n\nplus the final carryover 1 (millions place).\n\nSo the final number is 1 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, that would be 1,616,150?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let\'s write it as:\n\nMillions place: 1\n\nHundred thousands: 6\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo combining these: 1,616,150.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers directly.\n\nAlternatively, 856,321 + 759,829.\n\nLet me add 856,321 + 700,000 first? Wait, maybe breaking into parts.\n\nAlternatively, 856,321 + 759,829.\n\nLet me see:\n\n856,321 + 759,829 = (800,000 + 56,321) + (700,000 + 59,829) = (800k +700k) + (56,321 +59,829)\n\n800k +700k is 1,500,000.\n\n56,321 +59,829: let\'s add those:\n\n56,321 +59,829:\n\nAdding units:\n\n1+9=10\n\n2+2=4 + carryover 1 →5\n\n3+8=11 →1 carryover1\n\n6+9=15 +1 →16 →6 carryover1\n\n5+5=10 +1 →11 →1 carryover1\n\nSo 56,321 +59,829 = 116,150.\n\nWait, so 116,150. Then total sum is 1,500,000 + 116,150 = 1,616,150. Okay, that matches the previous result. So that\'s good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made an error in the digit-by-digit breakdown earlier but cross-verified here.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,616,150. Let me check once more step by step with the original digits.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n856321\n\n+759829\n\nLet me add each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 +9 =10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens:2+2=4 +1=5. So 5, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds:3+8=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThousands:6+9=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:5+5=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nHund